{"t": 1794118571.8540776, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "*PaymentGatewayErrors / checkout (OnCall AG-7731) \u2014 fix ready, needs deploy*\n\n*Symptom:* gateway 4xx rate ~38% on service=checkout since 07:41 UTC.\n\n*Root cause:* gateway API version 2026-11 (\"strict amounts\") now requires `amount` as an integer in minor units (cents). `checkout/gateway.py` was still sending a euro float, so charges were rejected: `HTTP 400 {\"error\":\"invalid_amount\",\"message\":\"amount must be an integer in minor units (cents), got 12.34\"}`.\n\n*Fix:* `checkout/gateway.py` `charge_payload()` now converts EUR to integer cents using Decimal with half-up rounding (12.34 EUR -> `{\"amount\": 1234, \"currency\": \"EUR\"}`). Verified locally across float and whole-euro inputs; no test suite in the repo (`pytest` collects nothing).\n\n*Next:* deploy checkout, then watch the gateway 4xx rate until the alert clears. I have not acknowledged/resolved the OnCall alert."}, "ok": true}
